  "notes": "SSH chain: end states\nThe Su-Schrieffer-Heeger chain: two sites per cell, whose hoppings alternate. The hopping modulation multiplies each bond by 1 - 0.3 cos(pi x) at its midpoint: 0.7 inside the cells, 1.3 between them. s1 is the infinite chain (its bands, c1), s2 a finite chain of 42 sites (its local density of states at zero energy, c2, and its density of states, c3). With the stronger bonds between the cells the chain is topological: a state at zero energy sits at each end. Exercise: change the modulation of both chains to 1 + 0.3 cos(pi x) (the stronger bonds inside the cells) and watch the end states go; then try 1 (no dimerization). The geometries and the calculations are locked.",
